Chapter: ChapterPages

 A chapter may legitimately span several files. Each file is a page and
 says so, and the pages agree: two of them, numbered 1 and 2, both
 declaring "of 2". The two halves merge into one chapter, which is the
 whole point of the idiom -- beta can see alpha.

 The three adversarial counterparts are errors/chapter-pagination-*.

Section: First
  alpha : Integer
  alpha = 1

Page 1 of 2

Chapter: ChapterPages

Section: Second
  beta : Integer
  beta = 2

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (alpha + beta))
  end

Page 2 of 2
